You're right--the "@" character is currently the most heavily overloaded 
in nethack, since it contains nearly all of the huge variety of humans, 
and all of the elves.  And yet TDT feels that blobs, jellies, fungi, and 
puddings are so different from each other as to require four separate 
characters to represent them all...

So unloading "@" is a good idea, and "K" is a good place to put some 
more monsters, but it shouldn't be done haphazardly.  Of all the "@" 
monsters, the ones most similar to the four already existing K-class 
monsters are the four types of soldiers.  The next most similar are the 
Minetown watch and vault guards, _except_ that they start out peaceful, 
which has enough important implications [1] to disqualify them from the 
K-class.

Shopkeepers seriously don't belong in "K" at all, because they have 
nothing in common with Kops except that both are human [2].  The ability 
to summon Kops is irrelevant; purple worms aren't the same character as 
shriekers, and spellcasters aren't limited to summoning other similar 
monsters.

> My logic is that the shopkeepers, minetown watch, and keystone kops are
> basically one team.

The shopkeeper is not on a team with those other two.  They don't work 
for him any more than real world police work for banks.  Sure, they come 
when he calls, but in theory they could respond to any type of 
lawbreaking that was coded into the game.








[1] They won't attack the player right away, but he has to be careful not 
to turn them hostile, and if they eventually do turn hostile, killing 
them counts as murder.

[2] YAOI: When a non-human eats a Kop, print "Mmmm... bacon!"


